                <pb facs="1240" n="1090" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg1090"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister O’Brien to
                        the Minister for Foreign Affairs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-03-02"><hi rendition="#italic">March 2,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>: Permit me to offer
                    personally, in advance of official congratulations, my most cordial
                    felicitations upon your election to the high office of Chief Magistrate of your
                    country. It is indeed an auspicious beginning which marked Your Excellency’s
                    induction into office, and I sincerely wish you all good fortune, happiness, and
                    prosperity to the Uruguayan people.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward C.
                    O’Brien.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
